@Comment:	child tends to speak with a rising intonation so many declarative sentences are marked with question intonation. It is often difficult to judge , both for the investigator and the coder , whether the child is asking questions or making statements. This should explain the apparent discrepancy between the pragmatic coding of the child and the investigator. This file is the continuation of Friend/F. There is an additional 5:00 of transcription.
